{"title":"1992 IMO Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906fddead65545297c74bbc2ca83cd01f3f9ecc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb{R}$\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" /> denote the set of all real numbers.  Find all functions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/f/7bfb1399ae9227b8c7b2b52ed47a508fd94de569.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f:\\mathbb{R} \\to \\mathbb{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"82\" height=\"18\" /> such that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/0/a903220090fd0b9b1f1bb19941c6d48abba8138d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f\\left( x^{2}+f(y) \\right)= y+(f(x))^{2} \\hspace{0.5cm} \\forall x,y \\in \\mathbb{R}\\]\" width=\"314\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>[quote=probability1.01]Set x = 0 to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/7/eb7ec6ef453d5708e9148527f639257210f3b28b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(f(y)) = y+f(0)^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"159\" height=\"21\" />. We'll let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/3/b93494b0887d69d9918b5acf33ea71cd4385ebbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = f(0)^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"75\" height=\"21\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/d/aad722e1647c101cbb8463559e7885a494715dbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(f(y)) = y+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"125\" height=\"20\" />. Then\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/8/ca804db7902475695594112f815e0108677ff2fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a^{2}+f(f(b))) = f(b)+f(a)^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"245\" height=\"21\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/6/6d6f47536714798d1d08453a56d8676fa1578d24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a^{2}+b+c) = f(b)+f(a)^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"225\" height=\"21\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/c/16c37c510aed240e09bb854b77ea8c58de599a41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(f(a^{2}+b+c)) = f(f(b)+f(a)^{2}) = b+f(f(a))^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"397\" height=\"21\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/d/f0d1882bbe1e0bce6465a25bdb6db60d7d84554c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^{2}+b+2c = b+(a+c)^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"204\" height=\"21\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/8/048b4fd55d275494735eaf090dcb27deb3c9972d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2c = c^{2}+2ac$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Since this holds for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/4/db496a2fade0867e2dedc83ca9cf6262560559a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />. Now we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/c/5ac19f76f21d9e784503af5e9e9abc8c3473bddb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(0) = 0 \\implies f(f(y)) = y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"212\" height=\"20\" />. Note that f must be surjective since we may let y vary among all reals, and f must be injective since if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/8/dd8989c314460e7bee5151e0dbf9f0ca3dd63338.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a) = f(b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/7/94770bfbd3500d8432bb992582c1f7dc2c8665d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+f(x)^{2}= f(x^{2}+f(a)) = f(x^{2}+f(b)) = b+f(x)^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"420\" height=\"21\" />. Finally, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/6/fb6b82881da23bf9b7daf1318c2e3c4609290a54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u &gt; v$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"10\" />, then there is some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> s.t. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/8/de88995761afc665c0de1a09dacac5602e5f0c17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u = t^{2}+v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"82\" height=\"18\" />, and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/6/7b66efca0642b49942be39982cc2744d750cfb2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(u) = f(t^{2}+v) = f^{-1}(v)+f(t)^{2}&gt; f^{-1}(v) = f(f(f^{-1}(v))) = f(v)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"532\" height=\"21\" />. Hence f is strictly increasing. It is now clear that since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/4/2b4b976dac854d591bb3a53136ebccfe9bd47f34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(f(y)) = y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"95\" height=\"20\" />, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/7/427c0ee5f10895f708b681a16c4f5799b31f41a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" /> for all x.[/quote]\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_IMO\" title=\"1992 IMO\">1992 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1992 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1992 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1992 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1992 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1992 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1992 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1992 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1992 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017183416\nCache expiry: 8640